<title>UK: UK notes in circulation rise 7.6 pct in week.</title>
<headline>UK notes in circulation rise 7.6 pct in week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>British bank notes in circulation rose 7.6 percent in the week of October 16 over the equivalent week a year ago, figures from the Bank of England showed. Last week the rise was 7.7 percent.</p>
<p>(figures in rounded billions of stg) -</p>
<p>			    Latest week  Previous week  Year-ago week</p>
<p> Notes in circulation  20.71	  20.77	     19.24</p>
<p> Bankers deposits	1.90	   1.85		1.73</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
